The tick hands the processor on without putting the preempted thread back in the round.
The thread would stay ready and never run again;
every ready thread but the running one is on the run queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a waiting or ready thread is on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -297,7 +297,6 @@ void sched_tick(uint32_t ticks)
     tick_advance(ticks);
     /* The running thread is ready, and goes to the back of the round behind any other that is. */
     if (run_queue != 0) {
-        ring_push(&run_queue, current);
         switch_to(run_queue_take());
     }
 }
